cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Bulwark, please cite it as below, and also cite the upstream models
  (docs/references.md) and every dataset the model you use was trained on
  (docs/datasets.md).
title: "Bulwark: a base video model for the state of a person on camera"
abstract: >-
  Research code for a base video model that predicts fatigue, distraction, attention
  and risky actions of a person on camera from short clips. Bulwark-B1 adapts a frozen
  V-JEPA 2.1 ViT-B/16 encoder with LoRA and multi-task heads; Bulwark-E1 is an
  EfficientViT-B1 student distilled from B1 and exported to ONNX.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-13
authors:
  - name: Inferensys
repository-code: "https://github.com/Inferensys/bulwark"
url: "https://github.com/Inferensys/bulwark"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - driver monitoring
  - drowsiness detection
  - distraction detection
  - video understanding
  - multi-task learning
  - knowledge distillation
